WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.520
We are here with philanthropist, activist,

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.429
oh, and Lady Gaga's mom, Cynthia Germanotta.

3
00:00:06.429 --> 00:00:08.069
(audience applauding)

4
00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:10.720
Okay, so if you're sitting at a table with her,

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.940
is there anything that you can think of

6
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.160
that she would say about how she sort of

7
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.810
matriculated that pain of the bullying

8
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.720
and the way that she felt,

9
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.420
into channeling it into something that was more empowering

10
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.000
and useful to her?

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.053
Yeah, I think she would say,

12
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.700
we talk a lot at the foundation about the impact

13
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.910
that kindness has on your mental health.

14
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.190
Not only kindness to self,

15
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.221
she talks about kindness on the inside

16
00:00:43.221 --> 00:00:45.150
and kindness on the outside.

17
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.260
And you have to be kind inside to yourself first,

18
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.873
before you can help...it's hard.

19
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.193
It's hard.

20
00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:53.026
Look away.

21
00:00:53.026 --> 00:00:53.859
I look away.

22
00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:54.840
I'm working on it.

23
00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.020
Do you have any advice for me?

24
00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.720
Baby steps.

25
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.059
Yeah, baby, love yourself.

26
00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.242
(audience applause)

27
00:01:01.242 --> 00:01:02.075
I'm trying.

28
00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:02.908
Love yourself.

29
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:04.813
Look in the mirror.

30
00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:07.720
It's okay to look in the mirror

31
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.130
and tell yourself that you love you.

32
00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.740
50% of mental health issues develop by the age of 14,

33
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.690
and that's about when it started happening for my daughter.

34
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.112 line:15%
But it's not uncommon for it to go undiagnosed for 10 years,

35
00:01:22.112 --> 00:01:25.620 line:15%
and I missed the warning signs.

36
00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.230
I didn't know what they were.

37
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:31.320
And you know, we talk to our girls and our children,

38
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.390
our boys too, about the birds and the bees, right?

39
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.080
We have that talk.

40
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.380
I call, we have to add the flowers and the trees

41
00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.610
about their mental health

42
00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.880
and having that conversation with them

43
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.040
in the same breath as the birds and the bees.

44
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.910
And if there was one thing

45
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.570
that I could leave with you or anybody is communication.

46
00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.680
And there's times they don't want it,

47
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.950
but communication to a fault, I would say,

48
00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.600
and it just keeps that dialogue open.

49
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.070
You know, one person in your life can make a difference.

50
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.190
And if that one, I used to tell my girls,

51
00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.000
I may not like everything that you tell me

52
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.420
but I would rather know and be able to help you.

53
00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.030
And so just having that one person in your life.

54
00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.510
And we found through our work at the foundation

55
00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:20.350
that it's life changing and it's lifesaving

56
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.090
in many instances if you have just one person

57
00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.190
that is there for you.

58
00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.190
I have looked forward to this conversation

59
00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.980
with all of my heart.

60
00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.330
I admire, like I said, you and your family.

61
00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.481
I admire what you're putting out into the world,

62
00:02:34.481 --> 00:02:36.210
what you're contributing to the world,

63
00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.150
how you're taking people in and making them feel safe.

64
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.010
And the Born This Way Foundation

65
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.270
is making a huge difference.

66
00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:47.590
And we're all also in love with your daughter

67
00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.650
and listening to her.

68
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.060
She's modeling a lot for us.

69
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.490
I know that's a lot of pressure,

70
00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.300
but she steps up to that plate.

71
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.590
So watching her be who she is

72
00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.410
is just a complete inspiration in every sense of the word

73
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.870
and I think there's such serious credibility

74
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.930
to what you and your daughter are doing.

75
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.330
So thank you.

76
00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.163
Thank you, yeah.

77
00:03:09.163 --> 00:03:10.503
Thank you so much.

78
00:03:11.676 --> 00:03:14.706 line:15%
Go to our website at TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com

79
00:03:14.706 --> 00:03:18.367 line:15%
to learn more about The Born This Way Foundation.

